## AC-5b — Teacher-forced gate (requires diagnostic build)

The teacher-forced mode is compiled only when `STRATA_DEEPSEEK_DIAG` is defined. For evidence capture it was built and run as follows:

```bash
# 1. Define the macro temporarily (not committed)
#    edit src/deepseek/ds_engine.cu: add #define STRATA_DEEPSEEK_DIAG before the #ifdef
cmake --build build-deepseek --target strata -j$(nproc)
# 2. Generate reference residuals and K/V (already produced for this run)
python3 /tmp/gen_teacher_inputs.py                  # writes /tmp/opencode/teacher_inputs.bin
# (K/V assembled from oracle_node_Kcur-/Vcur-*.bin)  # writes /tmp/opencode/teacher_kv.bin
# 3. Run the gate
LD_LIBRARY_PATH=/opt/rocm/core-10.1/lib ./build-deepseek/strata \
  --parity-run --native $PACK \
  --dump-layers /tmp/opencode/teacher_dummy.bin \
  --parity-teacher-force /tmp/opencode/teacher_inputs.bin,/tmp/opencode/teacher_kv.bin,/tmp/opencode/teacher_outputs.bin,$ORACLE
# exit 0
# 4. Compare
python3 $COMP --oracle $ORACLE --teacher-outputs /tmp/opencode/teacher_outputs.bin
# RESULT: PASS
# stage 1 (layers 1-27, 108 cells) max rel L2 = 1.569942e-04 at (layer=4, pos=3)
# stage 2 (layers 0-27, 112 cells) max rel L2 = 1.569942e-04 at (layer=4, pos=3)
```

After capture the `#define STRATA_DEEPSEEK_DIAG` was removed and the tree rebuilt; the normal binary refuses `--parity-teacher-force` (see `artifacts/diag_unreachable.log`).

